Virtio DMA helper — server-context provider for `vnet_va_to_pa`
================================================================

Second file of `module oskit.drivers.virtio`. Sibling alternative
to `virtio_dma_kernel.lsysl`. Exactly one of the two is linked
into any given build: the kernel image picks the trivial identity
provider, the standalone nic server picks this one.

When virtio-net runs inside the nic server, its ring pages and
buffer pages are ordinary server-owned pages — the server PT maps
them, but the device sees physical addresses. `svc_vm_v2p` walks
the calling thread's page table and returns the PA backing a
given VA, which is exactly what the descriptor rings need.

    module oskit.drivers.virtio

    import oskit.services.{svc_vm_v2p}

    vnet_va_to_pa(va: i64) -> i64
        i64(svc_vm_v2p(u64(va)))
